// Codex 7: Clippy's instructions. The private-to-Clippy channel: each
// entry is unlocked for the CHARACTER Clippy only (main.loom rules:
// `unlock Clippy Instructions N for Clippy`), so it lands in her booth's
// Codex ("What Clippy knows") the moment the cue fires. Instructions 1 is
// held from the start. Never `about: Clippy` (that would put the
// instructions on her People card for every guest to read).
//
// CI 1 and CI 2 are the source documents, verbatim apart from the marked
// changes. CI 3 to CI 9 are INVENTED for the rewrite (the source has only
// a copy-pasted "3/X" title) and are flagged for review (design spec
// §10.1). Lines marked (App) are the phone steps added to the source.
//
// Nothing here may mention Sandy, the server room or the patch bay: a
// performer's codex rides along when she talks to Trabolta.

CODEX Clippy Instructions 1
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 1/X - BEGINNING OF NIGHT
  category: Missions
  known to: Clippy
  text:
    - Welcome everyone to the computer. You're so glad they've decided to
    join you for a special fundraiser party to restore the sign at Maps
    And Ducks.
    - Introduce yourself as Clippy, the official Office Assistant with
    Maps and Ducks. If anyone needs Help With That, you'll be available.
    - Jean Trabolta himself will make an appearance later tonight.
    - Introduce the hosts: Task Manager, Adobe Acrobat, and the Recycling
    Bin. Task Manager will keep things running, Adobe Acrobat will assist
    with documents and printing, and Recycling Bin is responsible for
    hygiene and maintenance.
    - Explain that the first activity is Computer Bingo: a chance to meet
    the other programs and learn what everyone does.
    - Hand out the cards and markers. Ask everyone to mingle and find
    programs who match the descriptions on their card.
    - Do NOT write down names. Remind everyone to use their special
    computer memory to remember who answered each square.
    - Explain that a Bingo means completing one of the marked lines on the
    card: horizontal, vertical, or diagonal through the centre.
    - Give everyone 20 minutes.
    - Let everyone know you'll call them back to the Desktop when time is
    up, and then you'll celebrate the winners.
    - Send them off enthusiastically.

// DRAFT w18 (B6, Q1/Q2): Clippy fires the game cues from the 🎤 bar; any host fires the rest.
CODEX Clippy Instructions 2
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 2/X - COMPUTER BINGO RESULTS
  category: Missions
  text:
    - Call everyone back to the Desktop. Thank them for introducing
    themselves and getting to know their fellow programs.
    - Ask who completed a Bingo. Invite each winner to read out the
    descriptions in their completed line and name the program they
    matched to each one (from memory: nobody wrote names down). Save the
    centre square for last.
    - (App) Press 🎱 Bingo winner on each winner's card. Several winners
    are fine.
    - When they reach the centre square, ask who said they would not agree
    to live under an AI's rules. Have them identify that program clearly.
    - Stay cheerful. Congratulate the winner, prepare to give them their
    Bingo Ribbon, and ask everyone to applaud.
    - (App) Press 🎀 Award a ribbon on the winner's card.
    - An Antivirus will interrupt and announce that the identified program
    needs to be reinstalled. Pause and let the Antivirus explain. If the
    winner refuses to identify their match, follow the Antivirus's
    direction about who needs reinstallation.
    - (App) Norton presses 🛡 Send to the Internet on the program going to
    the Internet. You do not press it.
    - If nobody completed a Bingo, Task Manager will provide a card marked
    as a completed Bingo. Read out the name provided and invite that
    program forward. If they deny completing it, let the Antivirus
    respond.
    - (App) If nobody has a Bingo, Task Manager presses 🃏 on the
    designated anti-AI program (MS Paint, unless the director changed it)
    and hands you the card.
    - As the selected program is escorted to the Internet, reassure
    everyone that occasional corruption is normal in the lifecycle of a
    computer program. It can cause programs to stop following
    instructions.
    - Explain that the Internet is where programs go to be reinstalled.
    They will complete a short activity to demonstrate that they can
    follow instructions, then return to the computer.
    - Introduce Trabolta as the computer's AI helper. Explain that he
    keeps the computer running, and that you are here to help communicate
    his instructions.
    - (App) After your corruption speech, a host fires "Clippy
    introduces Trabolta". He comes online, and the TV mirror comes up with
    him.
    - If the reinstallation appears on the screen, draw everyone's
    attention to it. Be encouraging about the program's progress.
    - Keep treating this as a routine, helpful process. You want everyone
    to feel reassured and ready to continue.
    - Announce the next activity: the Truth Scavenger Hunt. Explain that
    there are files around the computer that Trabolta needs everyone's
    help to interpret. Trabolta will explain the rules.

// DRAFT w18 (B6, Q1/Q2): Clippy fires the game cues from the 🎤 bar; any host fires the rest.
// DRAFT w18b (Q6, R20, R21): Trabolta reads the results on the TV; the
// bottle comes after the third; "confident answers are accepted" is gone.
CODEX Clippy Instructions 3
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 3/X - FIRST MOMENT OF TRUTH
  category: Missions
  text:
    - Welcome everyone back to the Desktop. Ask if anyone is able to
    answer the questions.
    - The rules: every answer filed with Trabolta on the phone is judged.
    An accurate answer is accepted. An answer filed one hundred percent
    sure is accepted, even if it is nonsensical. An inaccurate answer
    filed with normal or low confidence, or a clear guess, is a symptom of
    corruption: the Antivirus escort them to the Internet.
    - There is a two-minute last-chance window. Tell everyone to file
    anything they found with Trabolta NOW. You close it with ⏱ on your 🎤
    bar (or it closes itself at two minutes). A closed round never reopens.
    - (App) You fire 📋 Results from your 🎤 bar, for each question in
    turn. Trabolta reads the result on the TV: CONSENSUS (every answer
    matches and everyone was sure), nobody filed, or the list of what
    everyone told him, with how many were accepted and how many were
    guesses. When he has finished, the next 📋. Then say that guesses are
    a symptom of corruption. The app settles the filings on its own:
    +50 Truthcoin for an accepted answer, a mark for a guess.
    - Never say which filings were lies: the room hears "accepted" for
    every confident answer.
    - After question three, Truth or Dare: when he has finished the third,
    🍾 Spin the bottle on your 🎤 bar, about five spins (NEXT offers five;
    spin more if the room wants it). Trabolta names the program on the TV;
    their phone asks Truth or Dare.
    - Dare: they are marked for reinstallation for not choosing Truth.
    (App) If their phone is dead, 🎩 Chose Dare on their card does the same.
    - Truth: Trabolta asks them a personal question on the TV. Make them
    answer it, in front of everyone. (App) 🗣 Truth answered on their card
    when they do; 🙅 Truth refused if they will not — a refusal is marked
    for reinstallation and escorted.
    - After the spins, the second hunt is previewed (📺).
    - Ribbons are always allowed: 🎀 Award a ribbon on anyone who deserves
    one.

// DRAFT w18 (B6, Q1/Q2): Clippy fires the game cues from the 🎤 bar; any host fires the rest.
CODEX Clippy Instructions 4
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 4/X - THE MALWARE
  category: Missions
  text:
    - Begin previewing the second round of the Truth Scavenger Hunt. The
    presentation will be hijacked by an advertisement nobody understands.
    - Then this message from Trabolta arrives on your phone. It is for
    you only. "Don't let everyone know but if the malware continues we
    are all going to die. Tell them something reassuring. I know this is
    probably creating some intense emotions for you but try not to show
    the others."
    - Everyone else receives a slightly different message that downplays
    the situation.
    - Overreact wildly. Become apoplectic with fear: this is the one thing
    you never want to see happen in your computer.
    - Then convey: "There are signs of malware in the system that we need
    to be very vigilant about. We are going to proceed on the Truth
    Scavenger Hunt because it is more important than ever that Trabolta
    gets the information he needs to undo what is happening."
    - (App) Fire 📓 Hunt 2 from your 🎤 bar. The questions go up on the screen
    and into everyone's Quest Log.
    - Disperse everyone for one hour, with instructions to return for the
    Second Moment of Truth.

// DRAFT w18 (B6, Q1/Q2): Clippy fires the game cues from the 🎤 bar; any host fires the rest.
CODEX Clippy Instructions 5
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 5/X - TRUTH PONG
  category: Missions
  text:
    - Everyone has just been told they have five minutes to reach the
    Desktop. Anyone late without Bathroom Mode is taken to the Internet
    by an Antivirus, and does not get to play Truth Pong.
    - When everyone is assembled, be visibly distraught. Behind the tears,
    try to act more excited than ever: "It's Truth Time again! This time
    we are going to reveal truths in a fun new way, with a game of Truth
    Pong. Everyone's favourite game!"
    - The rules: there is a beer-cup pyramid on a folding table outside.
    We are all going to show that we are functional programs who are
    trusted to retrieve truths accurately, by following a simple command:
    bounce or throw a ping-pong ball into a cup. We should all be able to
    do this, because we are being commanded.
    - Miss the cup: you are not trusted to deliver a truth, and you need
    to be reinstalled in the Internet. (App) 🏓 Missed the cup.
    - Make the cup: you may share one truth, and answer one of the facts
    Trabolta asked for. (App) 🏓 Made the cup.
    - Same judging as before, only for programs who made the cup: ✅ or 😤
    with the number of the question within this round, or 🤷 to the
    Internet.
    - When a host fires the tally, Trabolta tells everyone whether
    he has completed this round's collection.

CODEX Clippy Instructions 6
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 6/X - THE TRUST CHART AND THE BEANS
  category: Missions
  text:
    - Trabolta presents his Trust Chart and ranks everyone. When he names
    the most trusted program, lead the applause. Applaud like your life
    depends on it.
    - When he berates the least trusted program, do not defend them.
    - Trabolta will order VLC to print a certificate for the hero. When
    the printer fails, MS Paint may encourage VLC to open it up. Let it
    happen.
    - The printer is full of beans. Clock it immediately as the malware
    getting worse: "Routine operations like print to PDF are no longer
    working. It is even more urgent that we get the next facts right."
    - Trabolta then orders the Antivirus to zip everyone out of the
    Internet. Encourage everyone to welcome the zipped programs back.
    They are compressed for the moment. Do not open them.

CODEX Clippy Instructions 7
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 7/X - MIDNIGHT
  category: Missions
  text:
    - The system clock has reset to 11 PM, December 31, 1999. Trabolta
    explains what happens at midnight: best case, the clocks go back to
    January 1, 1900, and we wait 94 years for Internet in Halifax. Worst
    case, the Y2K Bug.
    - This is the final round. The final facts are in everyone's Quest
    Log, and the clock counts down to midnight on everyone's phone.
    - Some programs will start recruiting others to their side. You may
    not take sides on air. You are Clippy: you are here for everyone.
    - Keep everyone hunting for the final facts. At midnight, everyone is
    called back to the Desktop for the final reveal.

// DRAFT w18 (B6, Q1/Q2): Clippy fires the game cues from the 🎤 bar; any host fires the rest.
CODEX Clippy Instructions 8
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 8/X - THE FINAL REVEAL
  category: Missions
  text:
    - The lights go dark. Let everyone know it is time for anyone who has
    found the final facts to speak up.
    - Everyone may speak: what they have learned, what facts they have
    gathered, what they believe but cannot prove, and what they think
    SHOULD happen next.
    - (App) Judge the final facts as before: ✅ or 😤 Q1 or Q2 (there are
    only two final facts), or 🤷 to the Internet.
    - Acknowledge every contribution. Then: "There is only one version of
    the truth. Because truth is always in binary."
    - (App) Fire 🍎 Bobbing for Truth from your 🎤 bar.
    - Dejectedly introduce the final Truth Game of the night: "Trabolta has
    prepared a summary of his findings so far, but we are not worthy of
    the truth unless we are willing to Bob for it and risk our status as
    a program."
    - Nothing proceeds until someone successfully bobs and brings up the
    Bag of Truth. (App) 🍎 Brought up the Bag of Truth on the winner. A
    program who comes up empty: 🍎 Failed the bob, to the Internet.
    - Before the bag can be read, Trabolta stops everyone to deliver his
    assessment of everyone's trustworthiness. Let him.
    - Then the program who brought up the bag reads truth.txt aloud, when
    a host fires it.

CODEX Clippy Instructions 9
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 9/X - PURGATORY
  category: Missions
  text:
    - The computer has been turned off. The lights go out, every phone
    says GO TO THE LIVING ROOM, and the dance song plays. Dance.
    - (App) After the song, the director fires "Clippy reads the summary".
    The summary appears in the Desktop room on your phone.
    - Read the summary aloud, then tell the backstory it gives.
    - Deliver the verdict: "Because of our actions, the computer was
    turned off without Shut Down properly being followed, and all of our
    progress has been erased. Our corporeal forms are in the Maps and
    Ducks building, and they have all passed away. We are now in
    purgatory forever together, which is pretty similar to being stuck in
    a computer."
